hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"367","Narrated by Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sana'ani, narrated by al-Mu'tamir, who said: I heard Khaled narrating, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Anas, that he narrated: “They were looking for something with which to call the call to prayer as a sign of prayer.” He said: “So Bilal was ordered to recite the call to prayer and pronounce the Iqamah at the beginning of the prayer.”"
"368","Bundar told us, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, Khalid told us, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Anas, who said: “When the number of people increased, they decided to know The time of prayer was determined by something they knew, so they mentioned lighting a fire, or striking a gong, so Bilal was ordered to recite the call to prayer and make the iqamah Witr.”"
"369","Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Quti’ narrated to us, Ruh bin Ata’ bin Abi Maimunah narrated to us, Khaled Al-Hadha’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Anas bin Malik said: When prayer came during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a man ran along the road and called out: “Prayer, prayer, prayer,” and he intensified. That is for the people, so they said: O Messenger of God, if we took a gong? He said: “That is for the Christians.” He said: “If we took a trumpet?” He said: “That is.” For the Jews,” he said: “So Bilal was ordered to recite the call to prayer and recite the Iqamat Witr.”"
